  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-04-30T23:24:23.540Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "As a long-time VRChat user, I’d like to request a feature that allows us to choose who can send us friend requests. Ideally, this would work through customizable settings, such as limiting requests to certain trust ranks, friends of friends, or even by manually approving friend request permissions.\n\nThis feature is now more required by a vast user community. Content creators, VTubers, and streamers will likely have an infinite ocean of random or spam friend requests pouring in because they become searchable. It will kill their events, recordings, or live sessions. In the same way, normal users will be the victim of coordinated harassment, e.g., witchhunting, in which individuals receive spammed friend requests to scare them away or overwhelm them.\n\nWhile blocking users is one option, it's not an effective long-term solution. Harassers often create new alt accounts to bypass blocks and continue spamming friend requests, making it an ongoing problem.\n\nEarlier, the \"Do Not Disturb\" mode had helped somewhat by blocking friend requests automatically. But since May 1st update, the protection was removed. Ever since then, I, and other users, have been bombarded again with unnecessary friend requests, with no provision for filtering or managing them.",
